---
description: Performance patterns for tests: shared beforeAll and parallel setup.
globs: '**/*.test.ts,**/*.test.tsx'
alwaysApply: true
---

When multiple `it()` blocks in the same `describe` need the same expensive or
side-effectful computation, compute it once in `beforeAll` and store the result
in a `let` variable that each `it()` reads. This avoids repeating the
computation for each test case.

## Example

```typescript
// Avoid — each it() recomputes the expensive operation
it('returns annotated PDF', async () => {
  const annotatedPDF = await annotatePDFFormFields(pdfBuffer);
  expect(annotatedPDF.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
});
it('handles rich text fields', async () => {
  const annotatedPDF = await annotatePDFFormFields(pdfBuffer);
  expect(annotatedPDF).toBeInstanceOf(Buffer);
});

// Prefer — compute once in beforeAll
describe(annotatePDFFormFields, () => {
  let annotatedPDF: Uint8Array;

  beforeAll(async () => {
    annotatedPDF = await annotatePDFFormFields(pdfBuffer);
  }, 30000);

  it('returns annotated PDF', () => {
    expect(annotatedPDF.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
  });
  it('handles rich text fields', () => {
    expect(annotatedPDF).toBeInstanceOf(Buffer);
  });
});
```

## Timeouts

Use the 2nd argument of `beforeAll`/`it` for timeouts, not `jest.setTimeout()`:

```typescript
beforeAll(async () => { /* ... */ }, 30000);
it('handles slow work', () => { /* ... */ }, 15000);
```

## Independent promises

When a test starts several independent promises — fixtures, reads, or
assertions — use `Promise.all` instead of awaiting them one by one.

```ts
// Avoid
const stale = await FakeData.makeDBRedaction({ openedAt: hoursAgo(2) });
const fresh = await FakeData.makeDBRedaction({ openedAt: hoursAgo(0) });
await expect(getRedactionFile(stale.key)).rejects.toMatchObject({
  name: 'NotFound',
});
await expect(getRedactionFile(fresh.key)).resolves.toBeInstanceOf(Buffer);

// Prefer
const [stale, fresh] = await Promise.all([
  FakeData.makeDBRedaction({ openedAt: hoursAgo(2) }),
  FakeData.makeDBRedaction({ openedAt: hoursAgo(0) }),
]);
await Promise.all([
  expect(getRedactionFile(stale.key)).rejects.toMatchObject({
    name: 'NotFound',
  }),
  expect(getRedactionFile(fresh.key)).resolves.toBeInstanceOf(Buffer),
]);
```

Creating multiple independent fixtures with `Promise.all` is also covered
in `.cursor/rules/use-fakedata.mdc`.
